{"title":"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Algebra_Based)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Algebra Based)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Calculus-based)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Calculus-based)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(fake)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (fake)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the parabola with equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8ef862bdd16c2d5356e11735b8c766c402f5e10c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80ed80b5ab6845b9a5704ad0c613b3a44fd13d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = (20, 14)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />. There are real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> does not intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/834626cf7a247d2ad6f7a704749d7b072cd2ae08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &lt; m &lt; s$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"10\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317440729faba2b233a3547c42e9baccad52b82d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r + s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/7284938b19a365262927def7cf158eb35a9279b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 26\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 40\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 52\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"385\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Algebra_Based.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Algebra_Based)\">Solution 1 (Algebra Based)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Algebra Based)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83a009a3557281e83445a3f743f2c945e5f41788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = m(x - 20) + 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />. Equating them:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1ef05a9960a7925e7ad85b994e1c7899427b23a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = mx - 20m + 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbd2f33e55bc889bfde642b97d1846c18cf9ef18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - mx + 20m - 14 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"196\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>For there to be no solutions, the discriminant must be less than zero:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e786598a6dc44294e250e6e8033da906bffc7e04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - 4(20m - 14) &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f76c796cda833b169ac23e9fa23e2072eb84647.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - 80m + 56 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faff6ed3dfd43ddbdcefe376cb63d2e8c7cff628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/834626cf7a247d2ad6f7a704749d7b072cd2ae08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &lt; m &lt; s$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"10\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/0011af7dd6085598bd95a7102b63b508978db917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - 80m + 56 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" /> and their sum by Vieta's formulas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1c5158cdb86dc87452cbf7eb45a50134d3d6255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Calculus-based.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Calculus-based)\">Solution 2 (Calculus-based)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Calculus-based)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The line will begin to intercept the parabola when its slope equals that of the parabola at the point of tangency.  Taking the derivative of the equation of the parabola, we get that the slope equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />.  Using the slope formula, we find that the slope of the tangent line to the parabola also equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/442db8c25af2eeae7ba5b466dc946ca47daab2f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{14-x^2}{20-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"39\" />.  Setting these two equal to each other, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/4704bcc28878fd234d17a2f0c2cdc62c4a1b9b35.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x = \\frac{14-x^2}{20-x} \\implies x^2-40x+14 = 0\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"39\" />\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4fb8b4248a0f955aa5896f11568dfe028524e4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x= 20\\pm \\sqrt{386}\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />\nThe sum of the two possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> where the line is tangent to the parabola is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the sum of the slopes of these two tangent lines is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1c5158cdb86dc87452cbf7eb45a50134d3d6255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28fake.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(fake)\">Solution 3 (fake)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (fake)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The smaller solution is basically negligible in comparison with the solution with the larger slope. Try some values like of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8cbde33c95271b8839e9ad5e89e837c7bd09e76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2afae2c0f2b22fb6a5ad988d9ad4de951de80f69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> =&gt; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/4/e54a5634036c5788d6c019ced03f35ba8d02437c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 1600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />, and slope ~80. Trying a few values leads us to conclude the least possible value is around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca82661beb41678318228456081eabc9716ea78a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(E)}\\ 80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~Arcticturn\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B\">2014 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017205407\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 280/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6517/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.675      1 -total\n 59.87%    7.588      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.43%    4.871      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12432:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017205407 and revision id 221103. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}